                "senderName": "NWS Boston/Norton MA",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued November 6 at 12:54AM EST until November 7 at 10:00AM EST by NWS Boston/Norton MA",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southeastern Massachusetts, including the\nfollowing areas, Barnstable, Dukes, Plymouth and Bristol counties,\nand Rhode Island, including the following areas, Block Island,\nBristol, Kent, Newport, Providence and Washington counties.\n\n* WHEN...From 4 AM EST early this morning through Saturday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas. Storm drains\nand ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Periods of heavy rain today through Saturday morning may result\nin an area of 2 to 4 inches of rainfall across RI and Southeast\nMA, with a low risk (less than 30 percent) of isolated amounts of\n5 to 6 inches.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
                "response": "Prepare",
